---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure | TripAxle"
  description="How TripAxle earns money through advertising and affiliate links, and the line that money does not cross."
  heading="Affiliate Disclosure"
  updated={site.legalUpdated}
>
  <p>
    This page explains how TripAxle earns money, and the line that money does not
    cross.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising, affiliate links and sponsorship</h2>
  <p>TripAxle is a commercial travel publication. It can carry:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>affiliate links</strong> — where TripAxle may earn a commission
      from a qualifying booking or transaction, at no extra cost to you;
    </li>
    <li>conventional display advertising, and advertising sold directly;</li>
    <li>
      clearly identified sponsorships of the site or a section, and newsletter
      sponsorships if a newsletter is added later;
    </li>
    <li>media partnerships and legitimate referral or data partnerships.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Anything commercial is kept visually separate from the editorial guidance and
    labelled as advertising, sponsored, or a partner link. In the page code,
    commercial and affiliate links are marked <code>rel="sponsored"</code>.
    Ordinary links to airports, rental companies, and official sources are
    references and earn nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>The line</h2>
  <p><strong>Payment does not buy TripAxle's editorial conclusions.</strong></p>
  <p>So TripAxle does not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>accept payment for a favourable review, recommendation, ranking, or editorial conclusion;</li>
    <li>let a company pay to be described as “best”, or to be ranked above another;</li>
    <li>run paid editorial coverage without clearly labelling it as sponsored;</li>
    <li>let advertisers or partners write, rewrite, pre-approve, or otherwise control the independent guidance.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Which affiliate partners or commercial links TripAxle works with is a
    business decision. What that decision never touches is the advice itself —
    whether to rent at all, which approach fits your trip, and what to check
    before you book stay exactly as the guides say.
  </p>

  <h2>Where things stand today</h2>
  <p>
    No advertising or affiliate links are live on the site yet. This policy is
    published ahead of them so it is clear from the start.
  </p>

  <p>
    More on our approach in <a href="/about">About &amp; how we research</a>. If
    something reads like it was written to sell you a booking rather than help
    you make one, <a href="/contact">tell us</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
